course: dictionary
lesson: 3794
title: Forage: searching for food
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Forage is a word you will meet in science and in the countryside. To forage means to search around for food. «Scattering food in the grass makes gorillas walk and search, which is called foraging, and keeps them busy for longer.» The clue is search: the gorillas have to hunt around for their food, just as bees forage for nectar.
explain: Forage can also mean searching for something that is not food. «She foraged in his bag for a pen» means she searched around inside the bag until she found one. The context tells you which meaning you need: is it food, or is it a search?
explain: Forage can also be a noun, meaning food for animals such as horses and cattle. A farmer checks the forage in the field. When you are not sure, try the swap test: put "searching for food" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Forage (verb) means to search for food, especially as animals do in the wild.
fact: «Foraged» can also mean searched around for something, as in «foraged in his bag for a pen».
fact: Bees forage for nectar, and squirrels forage for nuts.
fact: Never eat wild berries or mushrooms unless an expert adult says they are safe.
fact: Forage (noun) means food for horses and cattle, such as grass and hay.
exercise: «Scattering food in the grass makes gorillas walk and search, which is called foraging.» What is foraging here? | *Searching for food | Running very fast to escape | Building a nest | Sleeping in the shade
exercise: «She foraged in his bag for a pen.» What does foraged mean here? | Gave the bag a kiss | Sewed a new bag | *Searched around for something | Ran away from the bag
exercise: On a farm, what is forage? | Tools for digging | A kind of tractor | *Food for horses and cattle, such as grass and hay | A type of bird
test: Bees forage for what? | Bricks | Tyres | *Nectar | Socks
test: Before you eat wild mushrooms, what must happen? | Your friend must taste them first | You must pick them quickly | Nothing, they are always safe | *An expert adult must say they are safe
exam: Which sentence uses forage as a noun? | She had to forage through the drawer | Families foraging for blackberries have fun | The squirrel will forage for nuts in autumn | *The horses ate the forage in the field
